# =========================================================================
#  Wind turbine DDP-HJB project -- what goes in the repo
#
#  Everything below still gets written to disk locally. This file only
#  decides what GitHub carries. The rule of thumb: commit whatever
#  report.html needs, plus the numbers; leave out the bulk.
# =========================================================================

# ---- MATLAB noise ----
*.asv
*.autosave
slprj/
codegen/
octave-workspace

# ---- OS noise ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# =========================================================================
#  Generated output
# =========================================================================

# Per-segment figures: save_segment_figures writes 4 PNGs per
# (model, segment). At 10 models x 190 segments that is 7,600 files for
# wind01 alone, ~1.3 GB across all profiles. GitHub's web UI becomes
# unusable long before that. They are regenerable -- set
# export_segment_figures = true in run_prediction to rebuild them locally.
wind_profiles/*/prediction/figures/*/

# Raw MATLAB workspaces. prediction_suite_results.mat holds every forecast
# for every segment and grows quickly with long profiles. Uncomment if you
# want the raw numbers versioned and your repo is comfortably under 1 GB.
# wind_profiles/*/prediction_suite_results.mat
# wind_profiles/*/control/*/control_results.mat

# ---- IF THE REPO GETS TOO BIG ----
# The full-resolution GIF tier is by far the heaviest committed item
# (roughly 1-3 MB per file, 20 files per profile). Uncommenting the two
# lines below drops ~40 MB per profile. The report still works: it loads
# the web tier. Only the "full resolution" links under each animation
# would 404.
#
# wind_profiles/*/prediction/animation/
# wind_profiles/*/control/*/animation/
#
# Alternatively keep them and use Git LFS:
#   git lfs install
#   git lfs track "wind_profiles/**/animation/**/*.gif"

# =========================================================================
#  Explicitly KEPT (listed for clarity -- these are not ignored)
# =========================================================================
#   report.html                                   the report itself
#   wind_profiles/manifest.json                   profile index
#   wind_profiles/report_data.js                  what report.html reads
#   wind_profiles/report_data.json                the fetchable twin
#   wind_profiles/*/README.md                     renders natively on GitHub
#   wind_profiles/*/summary_table.tex             for the thesis
#   wind_profiles/*/report/*.txt                  written report
#   wind_profiles/*/report/*.json                 machine-readable summaries
#   wind_profiles/*/report/*.csv                  GitHub renders these as tables
#   wind_profiles/*/prediction/web/               downscaled assets (the report)
#   wind_profiles/*/prediction/statistics/        the ten comparison figures
#   wind_profiles/*/prediction/figures/*.png      per-model timelines (not the
#                                                 per-segment subfolders above)
#   wind_profiles/*/control/*/web/                control assets
#   +windlib/data/*.csv                           source wind data
